<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tonglüshan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tonglushan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tonglüshan is an ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mine near Daye in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, worked from about the late second millennium BCE to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>. Discovered in 1973, it preserves shafts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> supports, tools and smelting furnaces, and the slag heaps suggest that tens of thousands of tonnes of copper were produced there. It supplied metal for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> China and later for the State of Chu.</p></div>
